## Symptom

The noop path records progress but never resets the in-memory wedge_counts/cooldowns (c2c_relay_connector.ml:3544-3556 vs the progress branch Hashtbl.remove pair at 3566-3571). A root that wedged at count 3, goes idle (registrations die, root becomes a noop), then re-registers and errors again resumes at count 4: up to a 2h cooldown for what is a first wedge of the new epoch, and the file and in-memory counts disagree until the next wedge.

## Fix direction

Perform the same Hashtbl.remove pair in the noop branch (or route both through one shared progress-reset helper).

## Evidence

Connector review 2026-09-17.